repository-code: "https://github.com/aswanth-07/matrixlang"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A compiler for a statically shaped matrix language with strict, bounded and
  algebraic numerical contracts. Grid and magnitude facts guide matrix-chain
  reassociation and reduction licenses. A separate rational-arithmetic checker
  replays numerical chain obligations conditional on supplied facts. ExactReduce
  applies related integer facts to selected reductions in LLVM 18. The artifact
  includes experiments, raw results, a technical manuscript, teaching exercises
  and a web demonstration. The manuscript states the numerical premises and the
  tested compiler integration's limits. No classroom effectiveness is claimed.
keywords:
  - compiler construction
  - computing education
  - domain-specific languages
  - type systems
  - code optimization
